          "derivation_summary": "Modeled water-surface elevation (m NAVD88) per Creek Segment. Discharge per NHDPlusV2 reach (NOAA National Water Model v3.0 retrospective, hourly, WY2021–WY2023; California Natural Flows, monthly, 1950–2024) is scaled to each Creek Segment by the USGS drainage-area ratio method (capped at 1; a segment on a creek with no NHDPlusV2 reach of its own uses Drainage-Area Ratio Transfer from the nearest reach, and gets no discharge beyond 1000 m), then converted to WSE with a divided-channel Manning's equation rating curve (n = 0.04 main channel, 0.07 floodplain) on USGS 3DEP 1 m cross-sections. Junction WSE at a shared vertex is the higher of the two neighbouring segments' values. Values are stored as Held WSE Intervals.",
