          "derivation_summary": "Modeled water-surface elevation (m NAVD88) and junction water depth per Creek Segment. Discharge per NHDPlusV2 reach (NOAA National Water Model v3.0 retrospective, hourly, WY2021–WY2023; California Natural Flows, monthly, 1950–2024) is scaled to each Creek Segment by the USGS drainage-area ratio method (capped at 1; Drainage-Area Ratio Transfer from the nearest reach, and no discharge beyond 1000 m), then inverted on divided-channel Manning's equation rating curves (n = 0.04 main channel, 0.07 floodplain) at the first, middle, and last USGS 3DEP 1 m cross-section of the segment, each with its own bed and a local bed slope. The middle (anchor) section gives the WSE (wse_m); the end sections give the water depth at each junction, shared with the neighbouring segment as the mean of the two end-section depths. The anchor point and the junction beds are static columns of the Creek Segments layer. Time-varying values are stored as Held WSE Intervals: a new interval starts when the anchor WSE or either junction depth changes.",
